Negative control for the picker opening on a real SURFACE (`R7-3`).

Has the picker state a background of its OWN. The class it passes reaches the ui
menu panel through `cn`, so tailwind-merge drops the panel's `bg-control-surface`
in favour of the consumer's `bg-transparent` and the menu paints no fill at all —
while keeping its portal, its ring, its radius, its position and every one of its
behaviours. The table rows and the status badges under it read straight through
the open menu, which is exactly what the operator was shown.

This is the CONSUMER's half of the defect, and the only half this lane owns:
`packages/ui` is import-only (`R7-15`) and its panel is already approved, so what
is left to prove is that the picker composes that panel instead of dressing it.
The failure mode is real and cheap — one utility in a styles file silently
withdraws the surface every other menu in the product has.

Apply from the repo root: `git apply <this file>`; revert with `git apply -R`.

Reds: the column-picker spec's panel case — the opened menu no longer carries the
theme's own surface, so it is not the same object as every other menu.

diff --git a/playgrounds/labs-nuxt/modules/scenarios/runtime/components/ColumnPicker.styles.ts b/playgrounds/labs-nuxt/modules/scenarios/runtime/components/ColumnPicker.styles.ts
--- a/playgrounds/labs-nuxt/modules/scenarios/runtime/components/ColumnPicker.styles.ts
+++ b/playgrounds/labs-nuxt/modules/scenarios/runtime/components/ColumnPicker.styles.ts
@@ -13,6 +13,6 @@ export default {
     // else is stated here: the surface, the elevation and the radius are the ui
     // menu panel's own, which is what makes this menu and every other one in
     // the product the same object (`R7-3`).
-    content: cva("max-h-96 w-56 overflow-y-auto")
+    content: cva("max-h-96 w-56 overflow-y-auto bg-transparent")
   }
 };
